# Real response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here. Astro's own `security.csp` emits a <meta>
# tag with per-build hashes for the inline scripts Starlight ships (the theme
# selector, mainly), and hand-writing a header alongside it would mean a browser
# enforcing the intersection of two policies that drift apart on every build.
# The panel — which is where a CSP actually earns its keep — is a separate
# origin with its own strict policy. See docs/cloud-sync.md.
#
# `frame-ancestors` cannot be delivered by a meta tag at all, so anti-framing is
# the X-Frame-Options header below.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Hashed, immutable build output.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
